SCENARIO:
ACS Consulting has all departments on a flat network. HR,
Finance, Engineering, and Guest WiFi all share the same
subnet with no isolation. A Guest WiFi user can reach HR
file shares and Finance databases.

SEGMENTATION REQUIREMENTS:
Each VLAN needs a subnet of its own. Your LAN already owns all of
10.51.{{ pod_id | int }}.0/24, so pfSense rejects any VLAN address inside it -
use the addresses below.

  VLAN 10 - HR Department
    Subnet: 10.61.{{ pod_id | int }}.0/24
    Gateway: 10.61.{{ pod_id | int }}.1
    Access: DC01 (DNS, AD), HR file shares only

  VLAN 20 - Finance Department
    Subnet: 10.62.{{ pod_id | int }}.0/24
    Gateway: 10.62.{{ pod_id | int }}.1
    Access: DC01 (DNS, AD), accounting app (HTTPS only)

  VLAN 30 - Engineering Department
    Subnet: 10.63.{{ pod_id | int }}.0/24
    Gateway: 10.63.{{ pod_id | int }}.1
    Access: DC01 (DNS, AD), internet, dev servers

  VLAN 40 - Guest WiFi
    Subnet: 10.64.{{ pod_id | int }}.0/24
    Gateway: 10.64.{{ pod_id | int }}.1
    Access: Internet ONLY (no internal resources)

YOUR TASKS:
1. Create VLANs on pfSense (Interfaces > VLANs), parent vtnet1
2. Assign interfaces for each VLAN (Interfaces > Assignments; the Add
   button only appears once a VLAN exists)
3. Configure DHCP for each VLAN subnet
4. Create firewall rules enforcing isolation:
   [ ] Guest cannot reach HR, Finance, or Engineering
   [ ] Engineering cannot reach Finance
   [ ] All departments can reach DC01 for DNS/AD
   [ ] Domain controllers remain isolated from Guest

